{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_eoil56njnsyacucakhgy4ep5pydhnlpojuyhijutpm5vvckfi5ha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — all gates pass.** One real bug found and fixed.\n\n## The bug (Phase B, CONFIGS row 15 / ERRORS row 6)\nThe C `md5_digest` takes non-`restrict` pointers, and its disassembly re-loads `m->a`/`b`/`c`/`d` from memory **before every one of the 16 byte stores**. So when `out` overlaps `*m` (well-defined in C: character-type stores may alias any object), the C produces a **byte cascade**, not a snapshot copy.\n\nThe Rust did `let md5 = *m;` once, then wrote 16 bytes → diverged at every overlap offset except 0. Fixed to interleave load/store per byte using `read_volatile`/`write_volatile` on `u8`, which also:\n- tolerates a misaligned `m` (the C doesn't check either), and\n- keeps null-pointer faults as **SIGSEGV** in *both* profiles — plain `*p` and `ptr::read_unaligned` carry rustc's debug-only null-deref UB check, which made the debug `.so` die with **SIGABRT** where the C gives SIGSEGV (second divergence, caught by Phase C).\n\n## Artifacts (`translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` inventory; C exports exactly `md5_digest`, Rust exports it too → **symbol diff empty**, 0 undefined non-libc symbols |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 9 rows. Mechanical grep proves the C has **zero** error returns/asserts/range checks/enums, so rows are the mandated generic boundaries: 3 null-pointer cases (fork + compare raw `wait` status), undersized `out`, all bit patterns, aliasing cascade, misaligned `m`/`out`, range endpoints |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 20 rows: no runtime flags exist; axes are field/byte/bit isolation, boundary values, prefill patterns, guard arenas, `m`/`out` sub-alignments (cross-product), in-place & every overlap offset −16..16, repetition, 4-thread reentrancy, over-large source |\n| `tests/common/mod.rs` | libloading harness — **both** `.so`s via `dlopen`/`dlsym` only; seeded xorshift64\\* PRNG; staleness guard (cargo does not refresh a cdylib on `cargo test`, which initially masked the fix) |\n| `tests/phase_b_valid.rs` | 19 tests, ~100k randomized cases |\n| `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` | 8 tests, incl. fork-based signal comparison |\n| `run_all.sh` | builds C + Rust, diffs `nm -D`, runs the suite for every feature combo × {debug, release} |\n\n## Gate status\n- [x] `nm -D`: 0 missing, 0 undefined non-libc\n- [x] All 20 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass under randomization\n- [x] No driver executable (no `add_executable`, no `[[bin]]`) → N/A\n- [x] All 9 `ERRORS.md` rows have passing differential tests\n- [x] Holds under every configuration: crate declares no `[features]`, so `default` and `--no-default-features` × debug/release all pass (30/30 tests each)\n\n`c_src/` unmodified (only the untracked `build/` dir added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":263,"cache_read_input_tokens":79434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":263,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79fb91f9-81f3-4a4c-8861-bc656a868b4a","uuid":"a4e5e54d-4bbc-402d-adc8-7a8f380c1962","timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:16:59.252Z"}
